KC builder (k27 tree scripts/kc-build.py): native kext placement largest first, best fit (KC_NATIVE_PLACEMENT=best-fit)

UniXNU-piano patches/k27-kc/0001, applied to the local k27 tree by hand (patches/k27-kc/README.md); docs/kc-space.md has the
measurements. With KC_NATIVE_PLACEMENT unset the builder places as before (first fit in link order) and its output is byte for
byte the same. KC_NATIVE_PLACEMENT=best-fit sizes every native kext's four segments with a dry link first, then places each
kind's segments largest first, each into the smallest gap that holds it. Either way the log ends the link with one "native
placement" line per segment kind (the headroom left), and a refusal names the kext. tooling/kc/build-kc-k27.sh sets
KC_NATIVE_PLACEMENT=best-fit.

Measured (k27 0059 kernel, the 26A434 KC base): main's 21 kexts: __DATA's largest gap 63.9 -> 81.9 KiB, __TEXT_EXEC's 2931.8 ->
3791.1 KiB, the rest unchanged; with Apple's USB host stack kept (PIANO_USBHOST_STACK=1) PianoTouch's 485.7 KiB __DATA_CONST,
refused by first fit (largest gap 470.2 KiB), links.

